6.  WHAT DISCRIMINATES THE READINGS
====================================================================================================
K22 PASS G_eff(0.05)/G_eff(0.2): pointwise 0.630; filtered 1.000; inert 1.000   ratio ~ 0.63 for (b), 1 for filtered
      the scale dependence is the cleanest discriminator: branch (b) boosts 5 h^-1 Mpc 60% more than 20 h^-1 Mpc; the filtered and inert readings are exactly scale-free. Measuring f sigma8 at two k at one z decides it, and so does the shape of P(k) at 0.05-0.3 h/Mpc
K23 PASS N(1e15)|(b)/N(1e15)|(inert) = 8868 at z = 0; sigma8: 2.27 vs 0.76   > 100
      sigma8 = 2.267 is not a 6% effect: with sigma(M) ~ 0.49 sigma8, exp(-delta_c^2/2sigma^2) changes by ~3 orders of magnitude at the cluster scale. Branch (b) is excluded by cluster counts alone, independently of any growth-rate measurement
K24 PASS f(0) = 0.4522 (theory) vs 0.5283 (flat LCDM); -14.4%; sigma8 = 0.7602 vs 0.811   |f(0) difference| > 10%
      on the literal beta = 0 background the growth rate is 14% below LCDM's at z = 0 and sigma8 is 6.3% low. That is the theory's real growth signature -- a background effect (H(0) = 77.3, Omega_m(a=1) = 0.2403), not an a0 effect. Testable with DESI DR2 at z < 0.6 where the errors are 1-2%

